{"tool_name":"ewas","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"EWAS","home":"http://www.bioapp.org/ewas/","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Epigenome-wide association study software.","addition_date":"2019-08-04T08:50:16Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:06:11.476086Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Desktop application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:EWAS","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"jiangyongshuai@gmail.com","name":"Yongshuai Jiang","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"kidney1979@163.com","name":"Fanwu Kong","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"xuliangde@hrbmu.edu.cn","name":"Liangde Xu","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"note":"Tutorial material","type":["Training material"],"url":"http://www.bioapp.org/ewas/service.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Regression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3659"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"EWAS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty163","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: With the development of biotechnology, DNA methylation data showed exponential growth. Epigenome-wide association study (EWAS) provide a systematic approach to uncovering epigenetic variants underlying common diseases/phenotypes. But the EWAS software has lagged behind compared with genome-wide association study (GWAS). To meet the requirements of users, we developed a convenient and useful software, EWAS2.0. Results: EWAS2.0 can analyze EWAS data and identify the association between epigenetic variations and disease/phenotype. On the basis of EWAS1.0, we have added more distinctive features. EWAS2.0 software was developed based on our 'population epigenetic framework' and can perform: (i) epigenome-wide single marker association study; (ii) epigenome-wide methylation haplotype (meplotype) association study and (iii) epigenome-wide association meta-analysis. Users can use EWAS2.0 to execute chi-square test, t-test, linear regression analysis, logistic regression analysis, identify the association between epi-alleles, identify the methylation disequilibrium (MD) blocks, calculate the MD coefficient, the frequency of meplotype and Pearson's correlation coefficients and carry out meta-analysis and so on. Finally, we expect EWAS2.0 to become a popular software and be widely used in epigenome-wide associated studies in the future.","authors":[{"name":"Duan L."},{"name":"Feng R."},{"name":"Hu S."},{"name":"Jiang Q."},{"name":"Jiang Y."},{"name":"Jin S."},{"name":"Kong F."},{"name":"Li J."},{"name":"Liao M."},{"name":"Liu D."},{"name":"Liu G."},{"name":"Lv H."},{"name":"Song X."},{"name":"Xu J."},{"name":"Xu L."},{"name":"Zhang M."},{"name":"Zhang M."},{"name":"Zhao L."}],"citationCount":21,"date":"2018-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"EWAS: Epigenome-wide association study software 2.0"},"pmcid":"PMC6061808","pmid":"29566144","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Epigenetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3295"},{"term":"GWAS study","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3517"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"EWAS","home":"https://bio.tools/EWAS","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Epigenome-wide association study software.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:ewas/app/www.bioapp.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"training_material":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":fals